	(text "CLOCK PADS -- LAYOUT RULE (TCXO_OUT, UWB_CLK0-3).\nA test pad on the clock network is a STUB, and stubs degrade exactly the signal this\ndesign depends on (1 cm of differential path ~ 10 cm of position error at 10 m).\nSo TP5-TP9 are NOT on the clock nets: each sits behind a DNP 0402 0R (R402-R406)\nwhose pad lies directly ON the clock trace. Default build = one unfitted 0402 pad on the\ntrace, nothing else. To probe: fit the 0R, measure with a ground spring to TP3/TP110,\nremove it again. If layout cannot fit all four anchor links, keep R403/R404 (A0/A1)\nand drop R405/R406 -- two is enough to compare skew. Keep the UWB_CLKx routes\nequal-length INCLUDING the R40x pad; never spur a pad off one channel only.\n\nSPI/IRQ pads: place on the trunk, not on a spur; one GND pad pair (TP111/TP112) beside\nthem so a logic analyser / scope can use short grounds.\nGND pads TP113-TP119: one per functional area so a probe ground is never > ~15 mm away."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 248.92 101.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "82040aee-0799-44f4-bedc-8adc4afd199a")
	)
	(text "nRF9151 system LED drive (D7)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 281.94 64.135 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "865df8fc-51b0-4a86-823a-ccab30a1d991")
	)
